the impact of the corona virus outbreak  is being felt all over the world even on  one of Indonesia's most remote  archipelagos in tunisians airlifted from  China's Hubei Province where the corona  virus outbreak began have been brought  here tuna tuna they're in quarantine at  the local military base gomorian ah da  we considered several places but we had  to consider the runway for the plane to  land and the facilities so in the end we  decided Natuna was the best place this  is the town closest to the quarantine  facility just a few kilometers away from  the military base decorations for Lunar  New Year are still up but the mood is  far from festive many here are angry  they weren't told about the quarantine  plan one second Appa we didn't know it  was happening  no one gave us any information all my  neighbors were confused the town is  quieter than usual that's because many  residents left when they heard the news  fearing for their own safety I left a  few days ago and then I came back  because I had to feed my chickens but  I'm still afraid of the virus the  evacuees are in quarantine here at  national for two weeks in total that's  the incubation period of the virus but  if any of them show symptoms of the  corona virus all of them will have their  quarantine extended the Indonesian  government says it needed to act quickly  and that meant there wasn't time to  inform the Islanders beforehand now  government employees are going  door-to-door telling residents there's  nothing to fear because the evacuees  won't leave the military base as the  initial panic calms down the local  Education Board revoked its decision to  suspend classes because of the  quarantine trying to restore some sense  of normalcy in the midst of a global  health crisis Jessica Washington  al-jazeera maternal
 

